    <item>
      <title>Tutorial: Themes and Workbench layout</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/tutorial-themes-and-workbench-layout/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/tutorial-themes-and-workbench-layout/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;With the arrival of version 1.0 it&amp;rsquo;s a good time to take a look at some of the basic appearance options available to adjust to our preferences. So let&amp;rsquo;s look at the basics of switching themes and changing the listing and appearance of workbenches in FreeCAD.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Tutorial: Editing the Light Source</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/tutorial-editing-the-light-source/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 28 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/tutorial-editing-the-light-source/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ve written numerous tutorials recently looking at some of the larger changes and developments in the upcoming FreeCAD version 1.0 which can already be found in the current release candidate and the weekly developer versions of FreeCAD. The recent tutorials include the &lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.freecad.org/2024/10/20/tutorial-on-view-parameters/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;On View Parameter&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; features in the Sketcher workbench and the new &lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.freecad.org/2024/09/30/tutorial-getting-started-with-the-assembly-workbench/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Assembly workbench&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Image Import Refactored</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/image-import-refactored/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 24 Apr 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/image-import-refactored/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Over the course of a few different PRs, developers @wwmayer and @PaddleStroke have re-imagined image import into FreeCAD. Gone is the old &amp;ldquo;Image Workbench&amp;rdquo; &amp;ndash; images are now first-class citizens in FreeCAD, with their import integrated into the core as a normal File-&amp;gt;Open or File-&amp;gt;Import. And this week @PaddleStroke implemented a new (and much more intuitive) user interface for setting the scale of an imported image. This is critical since the most common use of imported images is to match new CAD geometry to the scale in that image.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Radial Gradient Background</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/radial-gradient-background/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Apr 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/radial-gradient-background/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;For many years FreeCAD has supported a linear gradient background: at long last, developer @&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/xtemp09&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;xtemp09&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; has answered the frequent call for a radial gradient. Coupled with @&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/PaddleStroke&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;PaddleStroke&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;s rearrangement of the colors Preferences page, FreeCAD now sports an overhauled background option that is sure to make many folks quite happy. Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Little Things: Navigation Cube Update</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/the-little-things-navigation-cube-update/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Dec 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/the-little-things-navigation-cube-update/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;One of the elements that nearly everyone who uses FreeCAD has on their screen when working in 3D is the Navigation Cube. It provides a simple way of visualizing your orientation in 3D space, and serves as a simple way to navigate to predefined views (&amp;ldquo;Front&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Top&amp;rdquo;, &lt;em&gt;et cetera&lt;/em&gt;). A few weeks ago developer &amp;ldquo;adrianinsaval&amp;rdquo; (Adrián Insaurralde Avalos) submitted &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/7876&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;an improvement to the Navigation &lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/7876&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Cube&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that makes the corners much easier hit-targets, so it&amp;rsquo;s now easier to switch to isometric views of your model without going to the menus. Adrián was assisted in this venture by &amp;ldquo;Rexbas&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Jolbas&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;donovaly&amp;rdquo; (Uwe Stöhr), so if you appreciate the new, easier-to-use navigation cube, send your thanks their way.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Translating FreeCAD</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/translating-freecad/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/translating-freecad/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD is an international project featuring contributors from dozens of countries, and users around the globe. One way we work to improve the usefulness of FreeCAD is by making it available in many different user-interface languages using the crowd-sourced translation platform &lt;a href=&#34;http://crowdin.com/project/freecad&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;CrowdIn&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New in 0.20: Preference Packs</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-in-0-20-preference-packs/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 14 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-in-0-20-preference-packs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/releases/tag/0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FreeCAD 0.20&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; features &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/Release_notes_0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;hundreds of enhancements and bug fixes&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: the new &amp;ldquo;Preference Pack&amp;rdquo; Addon type allows packaging and distribution of any of the settings in a FreeCAD configuration file. The driving application for the new feature was the need to set font and color information along with setting the overall user interface stylesheet, enabling a complete, self-contained &amp;ldquo;theme&amp;rdquo; to be applied in a single button click.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
